  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Assistance to Vulnerable Displaced Populations in Northwest Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this project, IOM proposes to provide monthly cash for food and sensitization on nutrition to the most vulnerable displaced populations inside northwest Syria (NWS), thereby reducing the food insecurity and enhancing the nutrition of 20,750 (4,150 men, 4,150 women, 6,225 boys, 6,225 girls) internally displaced persons (IDPs) residing in 11 IOM-managed planned camps (PCs) in Idleb and northern Aleppo Governorates</narrative>
  </description>
